# Replace this file with the actual nudenet.tflite model binary (remove the .README suffix).
# The file must be placed at flutter_app/assets/nudenet.tflite so the Flutter asset
# bundler can pick it up.
#
# Model contract expected by NudeNetService:
#   Input  : [1, 320, 320, 3]  FLOAT32  (NHWC, pixel values normalised to [0.0, 1.0])
#   Output : [1, 2]            FLOAT32  (index 0 = safe score, index 1 = unsafe score)
#
# Obtaining the model:
#   1. Export NudeNet from https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet
#   2. Convert to TFLite:
#        python -m tensorflow.lite.python.tflite_convert \
#          --saved_model_dir=nudenet_saved \
#          --output_file=nudenet.tflite
#   3. (Optional) Quantise for a smaller footprint:
#        converter.optimizations = [tf.lite.Optimize.DEFAULT]
